      "text": "selleth all that he hath, and buyeth that field, Matt. 13:44. his lord commanded him to be sold, Matt. 18:25. sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, Matt. 19:21 (Mark 10:21; Luke 18:22). cast out all them that sold and bought in the temple, Matt. 21:12 (Mark 11:15; Luke 19:45). ointment might have been sold for much, Matt. 26:9 (Mark 14:5; John 12:5). Sell that ye have, and give alms, Luke 12:33. they bought, they sold, Luke 17:28. no sword, let him sell his garment, Luke 22:36. sold their possessions and goods, Acts 2:45 (4:34). Having land, sold it, Acts 4:37. Ananias … sold a possession, Acts 5:1. patriarchs … sold Joseph into Egypt, Acts 7:9. Esau … sold his birthright, Heb. 12:16. buy and sell, and get gain, James 4:13.",
